From e2cc82b3e886acef515563c5d7139d6ca8a26c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:03:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] GS worker: GIF packets processed off the EE thread

The GIF arbiter hands drained packets to one worker thread, which runs the
paraLLEl-GS tap and the CPU GS frontend for each in stream order (the
texture replacement still decodes from GS memory exactly as the packet saw
it). Packets with an A+D write the EE sees at once (SIGNAL, FINISH, LABEL,
display registers 0x59-0x5F) run on the draining thread after the queue
empties, so CSR bits and the GS interrupt keep their timing. GS public
entries, ga2_pgs::vsync and local-to-host reads wait for the worker first.
The worker is woken per 64 packets or by a sync. Only with paraLLEl-GS;
GA2_GS_THREAD=0 keeps the old path. GA2_PERF reports queued/inline packets
and time spent waiting.

Zettai ship map, 1x: game thread 54% -> 45% of a core at 60 fps (worker
14%), frames identical; at a 175 fps cap it holds 120 fps (143 iterations/s
at 175, was 124).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
